00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:13.334
with "Friends" and "The Bodyguard"-

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:14.167
- Yeah.

00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:16.173
- Leads to these huge moments.

00:01:16.173 --> 00:01:18.200
And I didn't know you were the
same kid. I didn't know that.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.100
And I'd seen you and so then
I was like, "Wait, what?"

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:20.933
- Yeah. (chuckles)

00:01:20.933 --> 00:01:22.397
- [Kelly] Anyway, so I had to ask.

00:01:22.397 --> 00:01:23.230
You're welcome.

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:25.210
But your stepmom is
Debbie Allen whom I love,

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:28.799
and your father is former
NBA player, Norm Nixon.

00:01:28.799 --> 00:01:29.632
- Yep.

00:01:29.632 --> 00:01:31.450
- So you went into the
entertainment industry

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:32.690
instead of basketball.

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:33.890
That was just the field you wanted?

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:35.130
- Yeah, that was the field I wanted.

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:38.490
And my stepmother was
always like, "Dance,"

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:39.750
and my dad was like, "Basketball."

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:41.947
She was like, "Dance" and "Basketball,"

00:01:41.947 --> 00:01:43.157
you know what I mean?
(audience laughing)

00:01:43.157 --> 00:01:44.700
But it was really my biological-

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.330
- You could have been like
the Harlem Globetrotter.

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:47.210
It's like a both.

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:48.360
I feel like they do both. (chuckles)

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:49.730
- Yeah, so my biological mother

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:52.610
and my grandfather used to
drop me off at the theater.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:54.780
Well not by myself, but
I went with my grandpa,

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.600
and we used to theater hop,
which we can't do anymore.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:58.837
People are standing at the door like,

00:01:58.837 --> 00:02:00.694
"Hey man, you got your ticket.

00:02:00.694 --> 00:02:01.527
- [Kelly] Yep.

00:02:01.527 --> 00:02:03.720
- But I remember just her dropping us off

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:07.180
at seven in the morning and
picking us up around like five,

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.000
and I would see all of the movies.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:09.833
- [Lisa] Wow!

00:02:09.833 --> 00:02:10.666
- Yeah.

00:02:10.666 --> 00:02:11.499
- And so that's kind of how
I got into the industry,

00:02:11.499 --> 00:02:14.500
and I started as OshKosh
B'gosh model so...

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.702
- Oh my God, I remember.

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:16.800
(audience applauding)

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:17.633
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:17.633 --> 00:02:18.890
- You're like bodyguard, Schmodiguard

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:20.327
- Yeah, bodyguard, Schmodiguard, whatever.

00:02:20.327 --> 00:02:21.210
- (laughing) Love it.

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:22.250
So speaking of your father,

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:23.690
so you play him in this series, right?

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:25.210
- Yep.

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:28.630
- One, do you audition for
that or do you just get that?

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:30.580
'Cause why would they make
you audition I feel like...

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:31.660
- I know, I know.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:34.827
But I actually wanted to
go through the process.

00:02:34.827 --> 00:02:36.789
- (gasps) So you did? (gasps)
- [DeVaughn] Yeah.

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:38.730
My buddy texted me. He was like,
"You should play your dad."

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:43.730
And I pre-read and got a call back

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:46.900
and finally I got it so...

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.224
- That's amazing.

00:02:48.224 --> 00:02:49.057
(audience applauding)

00:02:49.057 --> 00:02:49.890
Well that's kinda cool,

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:50.820
'cause then you had to
go through the process.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.217
But I mean, was that
weird for you to be like,

00:02:53.217 --> 00:02:55.050
"Hey dad, I'm playing you."

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:57.980
- Oh my dad, he's very non script, chill.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:00.130
And I remember telling him,
"Yo dad, I'm playing you."

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:02.019
And he was like, "Cool."

00:03:02.019 --> 00:03:03.289
(audience laughing)

00:03:03.289 --> 00:03:05.786
- Nixon, I bet he wasn't like,
"Don't make me look bad."

00:03:05.786 --> 00:03:06.619
- Yeah, yeah.

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:08.410
No, no, that actually
is one thing he said.

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:09.490
No, straight up, straight up.

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:11.020
He was like, "You not walking around

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:12.270
playing a fictitious character,

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:13.240
so don't make me look stupid."

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:14.987
- Oh my God, I love it. (laughs)

00:03:14.987 --> 00:03:16.160
I love that, I love it.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:17.670
Tell us about the show.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:18.930
- So the show-

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:20.810
- You look kind of hardcore in the clip.

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:22.133
- Yeah, yeah.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:25.700
The show, the most challenging
part about it for me

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:27.760
was my dad was very lean.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:28.593
He was skinnier.

00:03:28.593 --> 00:03:33.110
I was pushing 185, 190,
the physical aspect of it.

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:36.798
So I went through
intermittent fasting, HBO-

00:03:36.798 --> 00:03:37.631
(Kelly gasps)

00:03:37.631 --> 00:03:39.080
Yeah, they gave us meal plans

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:42.640
and we had a rigorous workout routine.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:44.177
- That's where I'm like, "Out."

00:03:44.177 --> 00:03:45.010
- We had practice.

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:45.843
Yeah, right. (laughs)

00:03:45.843 --> 00:03:47.070
You're like, "See ya."
- I'm sorry, "What?"

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:48.970
- So I mean yeah, that was
the toughest part for me.

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:50.828
'cause I'm thinking about pizza right now,

00:03:50.828 --> 00:03:51.680
you know what I mean?

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:52.513
- Yeah. (laughs)

00:03:52.513 --> 00:03:53.346
- [Lisa] (laughing) Oh my God. (laughing)

00:03:53.346 --> 00:03:54.179
- That's hard, to get you through...

00:03:54.179 --> 00:03:55.012
But I bet you felt really prepared though

00:03:55.012 --> 00:03:56.288
once you were doing it.

00:03:56.288 --> 00:03:57.121
- Absolutely.

00:03:57.121 --> 00:03:57.954
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:57.954 --> 00:03:58.787
- And it was great.

00:03:58.787 --> 00:04:00.490
I felt like I was in the
best shape of my life,

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:03.080
and I just felt good about
stepping into his shoes,

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:04.980
'cause I just wanted to do him justice.

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:06.550
- Has he seen it?

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:08.020
